<title>FRANCE: Italian carrier buys four more ATR turbo planes.</title>
<headline>Italian carrier buys four more ATR turbo planes.</headline>
<dateline>LE BOURGET, France 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Aero International (Regional) said at the Paris air show on Thursday it had signed deals to sell four ATR turboprop aircraft to Italian regional carrier Air Dolomiti.</p>
<p>The sale includes three of the most recent model, the ATR 72-210A fitted with 64 seats, and one ATR 42-500.</p>
<p>It brings to 13 the number of ATR aircraft operated by Air Dolomiti, whose routes include city-hopping flights between northern Italy and southern Germany or France.</p>
</text>
